  "body_markdown": "About us\n\nmeet Dr. ChrisMeet The TeamLivewell DifferenceOffice TourTechnologyJoin Our Team\n\nservices\n\ndCOEFull Mouth ReconstructionSedation Dentistry\n\nCosmetic Dentistry\n\nSmile MakeoverPorcelain VeneersNo Prep VeneersGum RecontouringTeeth WhiteningDental Bonding\n\nImplant Dentistry\n\nDental ImplantsSingle ImplantsImplant BridgesAll-on-X ImplantsLocator-Retained Dentures\n\nRestorative Dentistry\n\nDental CrownsInlays & OnlaysDental BridgesTooth-Colored Fillings\n\nOral Surgery\n\nBone GraftingRidge AugmentationTooth ExtractionSinus LiftWisdom Teeth Removal\n\nOrthodontics\n\nInvisalignBraces\n\nGeneral Dentistry\n\nPreventive DentistryPreventive CleaningGum TherapyRoot Canal Therapy\n\nTMJ TreatmentDental Emergencies\n\nnew patient\n\nfirst visit & new examInsurance & FinancingBlog\n\nOur work\n\nSmile GalleryTestimonials\n\nContact\n\ncall (703) 690-0102Request An Appointment\n\nBook Now\n\n703-690-0102\n\nLivewell Difference\n\nmeet Dr. Chris\n\nMeet The Team\n\nJoin Our Team\n\nOffice Tour\n\nTechnology\n\nServices\n\nFull Mouth Reconstruction\n\nDCOE\n\nTMJ Treatment\n\nDental Emergencies\n\nSedation Dentistry\n\nPreventive\n\nDental Bridges\n\nRoot Canal\n\nProfessional Dental Cleaning\n\nScaling & Root Planing\n\nAll General Dentistry services\n\nSmile Makeover\n\nPorcelain Veneers\n\nNo Prep Veneers\n\nTeeth Whitening\n\nGum Recontouring\n\nAll Cosmetic Dentistry Services\n\nSingle Implants\n\nImplant Bridges\n\nAll-on-X Implants\n\nLocator-Retained Dentures\n\nAll Implant Dentistry Services\n\nWisdom Teeth Removal\n\nTooth Extraction\n\nSinus Lift\n\nBone Grafting\n\nRidge Augmentation\n\nInvisalign\n\nBraces\n\nAll Orthodontics Services\n\nDental Crowns\n\nTooth-Colored Fillings\n\nDental Bonding\n\nInlays & Onlays\n\nAll Restorative Dentistry Services\n\nNew Patient\n\nfirst visit & new exam\n\nInsurance & Financing\n\nBlog\n\nTestimonials\n\nSmile Gallery\n\nCALL US: (703) 690-0102\n\nBOOK AN APPOINTMENT\n\n320+\n\n5 Star Reviews\n\n\n# Sinus Lift in Fairfax Station, VA\n\n\nPlanned for your future implant\n\nAdvanced imaging for safer planning\n\nComfort-focused surgical approach\n\n\n## What Is a Sinus Lift?\n\n\nA sinus lift is a bone grafting procedure for the upper back jaw, usually near the molars and premolars.\n\nWhen teeth have been missing in this area, the bone can shrink over time. At the same time, the sinus cavity may sit lower, leaving limited space for a dental implant.\n\nDuring a sinus lift, the sinus membrane is gently lifted and bone grafting material is placed underneath it. As the area heals, new bone forms and creates stronger support for a future implant.\n\nFor many patients, a sinus lift makes implant treatment possible when there was not enough bone before.\n\n\n## Are You a Candidate?\n\n\nThis could be right for you if you have:\n\nMissing upper back teeth\n\n‍Bone loss is common after molars or premolars have been missing for a long time.\n\nBeen told you do not have enough bone for an implant\n\n‍A sinus lift can help create the vertical bone height needed for implant placement.\n\nA sinus that sits close to the jawbone\n\n‍Some patients naturally have less space between the sinus and upper jaw, even before tooth loss.\n\nA plan for upper dental implants\n\n‍If implants are part of your future smile plan, a sinus lift may be the step that helps make them possible.\n\n\n## Benefits of Sinus Lift\n\n\n\n### Makes Dental Implants Possible\n\n\nCreates bone height in the upper back jaw where implants may not have been possible before.\n\n\n### Restores Jawbone Structure\n\n\nHelps rebuild the foundation that may have changed after tooth loss, infection, or long-term bone shrinkage.\n\n\n### Provides Strong Implant Support\n\n\nA healthier bone foundation can help implants feel more stable, functional, and natural over time.\n\n\n## The Sinus Lift Process\n\n\nHere’s what you can expect.\n\nConsultation & 3D Imaging\n\nWe begin with a detailed exam and digital imaging to evaluate your sinus position, bone height, and implant options.\n\nPersonalized Treatment Plan\n\nDr. Chris explains whether a sinus lift is needed, how it fits into your implant plan, and what to expect before treatment begins.\n\nGentle Sinus Elevation\n\nThe sinus membrane is carefully lifted to create space for new bone support in the upper jaw.\n\nBone Graft Placement\n\nGrafting material is placed beneath the sinus membrane to help rebuild the area where support is needed.\n\nHealing & Implant Readiness\n\nOver time, your body integrates the graft. Once the area is ready, we can move forward with implant placement or the next phase of your plan.\n\n\n## Sinus Lift Treatment With a Clear Plan, Not Guesswork\n\n\nAt Livewell Dental, a sinus lift is never planned in isolation. We look at your sinus anatomy, bone levels, bite, gum health, implant position, and final restoration before recommending treatment.\n\nOur goal is to help you understand why the procedure may be needed and how it supports a stronger, healthier, more confident smile.\n\nWhy patients choose Livewell:\n\nAdvanced imaging for precise planning\n\nA comfort-first approach to surgical care\n\nClear explanations before treatment begins\n\nPersonalized treatment based on your anatomy and goals\n\nA focus on long-term function, health, and aesthetics\n\nMEET DR. CHRIS\n\n\n## Stronger Bone for Your Implants, With an Easier Recovery\n\n\nPlatelet-Rich Fibrin (PRF), Drawn From Your Own Blood\n\nA sinus lift adds bone in the delicate space beneath your sinus membrane so it can support future implants. We spin a small sample of your blood chairside and blend the resulting PRF into the graft. Its concentrated growth factors speed new bone formation, help protect the membrane, and calm inflammation, so the site integrates more predictably.\n\nHelps the graft mature into solid bone that can anchor implants\n\nSupports and protects the sinus membrane while it heals\n\nEases post-operative swelling and discomfort\n\nComes entirely from your own body, so there is nothing to reject\n\n\n## Trusted by Patients Who Want Their Smile Done Right\n\n\nPatients choose Livewell Dental because they want thoughtful planning and honest guidance. A sinus lift is often one step in a larger implant plan, and we take the time to make sure each step supports your final result.\n\nWhether you have been told you do not have enough bone or you are just starting to explore dental implants, our team will help you move forward with clarity and confidence.\n\nschedule a consultation\n\nWhy would I need a sinus lift?\n\nYou may need a sinus lift if there is not enough bone in the upper back jaw to safely support a dental implaint.\n\nIs a sinus lift the same as bone grafting?\n\nA sinus lift is a specific type of bone grafting. It is used in the upper back jaw when more bone height is needed near the sinus.\n\nDoes a sinus lift hurt?\n\nWe use local anesthesia and a comfort-focused approach during treatment. Some soreness, swelling, or pressure afterward is normal and usually manageable with post-care instructions.\n\nHow long does a sinus lift take to heal?\n\nHealing time varies depending on your anatomy and the amount of grafting needed. Many patients need a few months of healing before implant placement.\n\nCan I get an implant at the same time as a sinus lift?\n\nSometimes, yes. If there is enough existing bone stability, the dental implant may be placed during the same visit. If not, the graft will need time to heal first.\n\nHow is a sinus lift different from ridge augmentation?\n\nA sinus lift adds bone height in the upper back jaw near the sinus. Ridge augmentation rebuilds the width or shape of the jaw ridge after bone loss. Both procedures can help prepare the mouth for implants, but they solve different bone problems.\n\nHow much does a sinus lift cost?\n\nA sinus lift typically runs $500 to $2,500. Pricing depends on whether one or both sides need treatment, the graft material used, and the complexity of the case.\n\n\n## Frequently Asked Questions About Sinus Lift Treatment\n\n\n\n### Reimagine your dental experience\n\n\n\n### address\n\n\n9027 Silverbrook Rd Ste. F\n\nFairfax Station, VA 22039\n\n\n### Contact\n\n\n\n### Hours\n\n\nMon-Tue: 8am-5pm\n\nWed-Thu: 8am-4pm\n\nFri: 8am-1pm\n\n\n### Connect\n\n\nServing Fairfax Station and the Greater Northern Virginia Area\n\nCopyright © TEXT-YEAR Livewell Dental\n\nPrivacy Policy\n\nTerms of Service\n\nCookie Policy\n\nHIPAA Disclosure\n\nConsent Preferences",
